        "title": "fix(ui): remove redundant esc label in file preview modal header",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Skill Workshop file preview displayed two Escape hints: a non-actionable badge beside the file count and the useful shortcut hint on the Close button.\n\nFixes #99027.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe header is status-only, so its nested Escape badge suggested an action where none exists. This focused change removes that badge and its now-unused styles while preserving the actual Escape key handler and the Close-button shortcut hint.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe file preview header now shows only the file count. The footer continues to show `Close esc`, and pressing Escape still closes the dialog.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwtdcpm4pefrxn940m0gy2mf`:\n  - `corepack pnpm test ui/src/components/file-preview-modal.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 5 tests passed.\n- In-app browser, real `openclaw-file-preview-modal` component imported from this exact checkout:\n  - dialog role: `dialog`;\n  - header state: `2 files`;\n  - header Escape/KBD count: `0`;\n  - close control: `Close esc`, with its `.kbd` text still `esc`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh final branch autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nThe maintainer refresh rebases the contributor patch onto current `main`, follows the component’s new path, adds focused regression coverage, and adds changelog credit.\n",
